 "priority": 2,
 "source_bins": [
  "sound_auth.bin",
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "So, we know the corpse was removed\nwithout anyone noticing.": "",
  "And that's...\nin Okubo-kun's laundry bin.": "",
  "And Okubo-kun had his laundry cart.\nIt would have been a perfect hiding place.": "",
  "The victim was in his room one minute\nand then gone the next.": "",
  "The window doesn't open,\nso the only way out is through the door.": "",
  "His window didn't open, so the only way he could\nhave been taken out was through the door.": "",
  "No one saw him leave though, even though\nthere are always people in the halls.": "",
  "But nobody saw that happen, even though\nthere were people in the hallway.": "",
  "And the only one who entered the room\nwas Okubo with his laundry cart.": "",
  "And the only one who went in the victim's room\nwas Shinpei Okubo with his laundry cart.": "",
  "Hey, I don't wanna be a downer... \nBut doesn't that point to Okubo being the killer?": "",
  "Right. Not to interrupt you, of course, but...\ndoesn't that point to Okubo being the killer?": "",
  "What the hell's your problem!?": "",
  "Hey! What the hell's your problem!?": "",
  "Was that Shintani!?": "",
  "Hold on, isn't that Shintani?": "",
  "I think so!": "",
  "That bastard...\nwas eavesdropping on you...": "",
  "I tried to stop him,\nbut he pulled a stun gun on me...": "",
  "Yeah... I tried to stop him,\nbut he pulled a stun gun on me...": "",
  "Wait up!": "",
  "A woman...?": "",
  "Help!\nSomeone help me!": "",
  "Somebody help!\nI'm getting molested!": "",
  "Aren't you... Terasawa-san!?": "",
  "Wait, you're Terasawa-san!\nAren't you?": "",
  "Let go of me!": "",
  "We got a groper out here!?\nScum of the earth!": "",
  "Groping a pretty young lady in public, huh?\nYou scumbag!": "",
  "Not on my watch,\nyou son of a bitch!": "",
  "You're gonna pay for that! Come on!": "",
  "Can all lawyers fight like that?": "",
  "Did you really need to run away like that?": "",
  "Did you really need to run away?": "",
  "I assume you came to see me.": "",
  "There was something I wanted to talk to you\nabout, yes... but I wasn't sure if I should.": "",
  "I did want to talk to you about something, Yagami-san...\nbut I wasn't sure if I should.": "",
  "Then that pigheaded friend of yours\nstarted shouting, so I just lost it...": "",
  "Then that pigheaded friend of yours\nstarted shouting, and...": "",
  "Okay, but did you have to tase him?": "",
  "The stun gun was a little over the top...": "",
  "Not that he didn't have it coming.": "",
  "Still... If anyone deserved it, it's him.": "",
  "Anyway.\nI'm listening if you wanna talk.": "",
  "Anyway, I'm listening if you wanna talk.": "",
  "No matter what it is,\nI'll keep your secret.": "",
  "No matter what it is, I'll keep your secret.": "",
  "Anything you tell me will fall\nunder client-attorney privilege.": "",
  "It's my job. Lawyers are sworn\nto confidentiality.": "",
  "Well, you know the witness\nwho last saw Waku-san?": "",
  "Said he saw him sleeping in his bed.": "",
  "Well, that witness is a man\nby the name of Shono-san.": "",
  "I can tell you more. That witness is a man\nby the name of Shono-san.": "",
  "He's one of the scientists at the ADDC. Not only that,\nbut he's the director's right-hand man, too.": "",
  "He's one of the scientists at the ADDC.\nAnd the director's right-hand man.": "",
  "And this is him?": "",
  "That's Shono?": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(Pretty much your run-of-the-mill researcher.)</color>": "",
  "Yes. He's a very dedicated doctor,\nso the nurses have a lot of faith in him.": "",
  "Yes. The nurses at the ADDC say\nhe's a reliable, diligent worker.": "",
  "But something felt off when I heard\nwhat he had to say about the incident.": "",
  "But when I listened to his testimony,\nsomething about it didn't feel right.": "",
  "I guess I'm just skeptical as to whether\nor not he actually saw Waku-san.": "",
  "I'm not sure he really saw Waku-san.\nSomething doesn't make sense.": "",
  "I don't think he's intentionally deceiving us...\nBut he may be mistaken somehow.": "",
  "I don't think he's intentionally deceiving us, but...\nhe may be mistaken somehow.": "",
  "And if I had to guess,\nI'd say the other nurses feel the same.": "",
  "And if I had to guess,\nI'd say the other nurses agree with me.": "",
  "Still, why hasn't anyone mentioned\nthis until now?": "",
  "Nobody mentioned any of this before.": "",
  "How could we? Nurses talking about\na doctor behind his back?": "",
  "Doesn't it feel like talking behind\na doctor's back?": "",
  "That's not something a nurse could do without consequences.\nAnd if it came to a courtroom testimony...": "",
  "For a nurse especially, that's a scary prospect.\nAnd if it came to a courtroom testimony...": "",
  "None of you would testify?": "",
  "You wouldn't testify, Terasawa-san?": "",
  "Maybe the other nurses wouldn't, but I would.\nI never really fit in over there anyway. Besides...": "",
  "...I could. I never really fit in there\nanyway. Besides...": "",
  "I think Okubo-san is innocent.": "",
  "Oh really? Sounds like I've\nfinally got an ally on my team.": "",
  "Oh yeah? Nice.\nGuess we're on the same team, then.": "",
  "I'm currently employed as a researcher\nat the Advanced Drug Development Center.": "",
  "Part of our research consists of clinical tests\nwe perform on patients in the general ward of the center.": "",
  "Part of the ADDC's research consists of clinical tests\nwe perform on patients in the general ward.": "",
  "On the day of the crime, I was making\nmy usual rounds through the ward.": "",
  "So, on the day of the crime,\nI was making my usual rounds through the ward.": "",
  "And what time was that?": "",
  "Around 7:50.": "",
  "Yes. The patients eat breakfast\nat precisely 8 o' clock.": "",
  "Yes, the patients eat breakfast\nat precisely 8 o'clock.": "",
  "I always head to the break room\nmyself right around then, too.": "",
  "It's not an unusual occurrence... I always head to the floor's\nday room myself right around then, too.": "",
  "This break room, to be precise?": "",
  "The \"day room\" being this one?": "",
  "That's correct. Our more mobile patients walk there\nfor breakfast instead of eating in their own rooms.": "",
  "That's correct. Our more mobile patients walk there for breakfast\ninstead of eating in their own rooms.": "",
  "Then while the nurses help the patients eat, I ask about\nhow they feel and how the medicine is treating them.": "",
  "Then while the nurses help the patients eat,\nI ask about how they feel and how the medicine is treating them.": "",
  "And on the day of Waku-san's disappearance,\nyou passed by his room before going to the break room?": "",
  "And on the day of Waku-san's disappearance, Shono-san,\nyou passed by his room before going to the break room?": "",
  "And in that room,\nyou saw Waku-san lying on the bed.": "",
  "And in that room, you saw Waku-san\nlying on the bed.": "",
  "Can you describe the situation\nto us as you remember it?": "",
  "Can you describe the situation to us\nas you remember it?": "",
  "The door has a window, so you can see\ninto the room from the hallway.": "",
  "There's a window on the hospital room's doors,\nso you can see inside from the hallway.": "",
  "And this is the room\nyou're referring to, yes?": "",
  "And this is the room you're referring to?": "",
  "From where I was standing in the hallway,\nI could see Waku-san lying in bed.": "",
  "From the hallway,\nI could see Waku-san in his room.": "",
  "He was asleep, with a blanket\ncovering most of his body.": "",
  "Waku-san had a blanket over himself.\nHe was asleep in his bed.": "",
  "No further questions.": "",
  "Yagami-sensei.\nWhy did you call her to the stand?": "",
  "Yagami-sensei... What's she doing here?\nWhy did you call her to the stand?": "",
  "She actually asked to testify.\nIs that a problem?": "",
  "Not really, no.": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(Here's my chance for a comeback!)</color>": "",
  "Terasawa-san. You were present for Shono-san's\ntestimony just now, yes?": "",
  "Terasawa-san. You were present for\nShono-san's testimony just now, yes?": "",
  "And what is your opinion\non that testimony?": "",
  "And what is your opinion on that testimony?": "",
  "For a scientist,\nI felt his wording was rather imprecise.": "",
  "And as a medical professional,\nI felt his actions were negligent.": "",
  "Could I ask you to be\na little more specific?": "",
  "Could I ask you to be more specific?": "",
  "Our witness, Shono-san, claims he saw Waku-san\nsleeping in his bed during his morning rounds.": "",
  "According to Shono-san, he saw Waku-san\nsleeping under a blanket in his bed.": "",
  "However, there's no way he could have known\nthat just by looking in from the hallway.": "",
  "However... there's no way he could have known that\njust by looking in from the hallway.": "",
  "And why do you say that, Terasawa-san?": "",
  "Can you explain why?": "",
  "The head of the bed is obstructed\nby the large cabinet in the room.": "",
  "You wouldn't know if the patient was asleep\nunless you walked into the room yourself.": "",
  "I have evidence supporting\nTerasawa-san's testimony.": "",
  "I have supporting evidence for\nTerasawa-san's testimony.": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(Shono shouldn't have been able to see Waku.\nI have evidence to prove that.)</color>": "",
  "Take a look at this if you would.": "",
  "Please look at this.": "",
  "And this is...?": "",
  "Ah, well it's an important piece of evidence, but the truly\nvital part is what I'm going to show you next.": "",
  "...Well, it's an important piece of evidence,\nbut the vital part is what I'm going to show you next.": "",
  "It's a photograph of the victim's room,\nas viewed from the hallway.": "",
  "It's a photograph of the victim's room\nas viewed from the hallway door.": "",
  "In other words, this is what Shono-san\nwould have seen when he checked in on Waku-san.": "",
  "In other words, this is what Shono-san would have seen\nwhen he checked in on Waku-san.": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(And this evidence points to this fact...)</color>": "",
  "Waku-san was already dead\nwhen Shono-san went to check on him.": "",
  "The victim was already dead\nwhen Shono-san saw him.": "",
  "What are you implying?": "",
  "Huh...? What are you talking about?": "",
  "At the time, the defendant hadn't yet collected\nthe linens. In fact, he hadn't even arrived at the ADDC.": "",
  "At the time, the defendant hadn't gathered the linens.\nHe hadn't even arrived at the Center.": "",
  "Meaning Okubo-san could not\nhave been the murderer. ": "",
  "Which means the murderer was not the defendant,\nbut someone else entirely.": "",
  "Assuming that's true, then...": "",
  "If the defendant isn't the killer...": "",
  "Why did he go through the trouble of hiding\nWaku-san's body in his laundry cart?": "",
  "...then why did he go to the trouble of hiding the body\nin his laundry cart and taking it out of the room?": "",
  "Huh? Well, depending on how you look at it...": "",
  "Huh? Well, you see, that's... Um...": "",
  "Please. You know this is\na court of law, don't you?": "",
  "Do you even understand\nwhat you're saying?": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(Shoot, I have to calm down.\nLet's try this again!)</color>": "",
  "The murderer was already\nhiding in the room.": "",
  "The killer was hiding in the room.": "",
  "He then killed Waku-san after Shono-san left.": "",
  "Then, they killed the victim\nafter Shono-san left.": "",
  "After that, he used a laundry cart to carry\nthe body down to Okubo-san's truck in the garage.": "",
  "They used a laundry cart to hide the body,\nand take it to the truck in the parking garage.": "",
  "But there was only one person seen taking\na laundry cart from Waku-san's room...": "",
  "C'mon! The person who took the laundry cart\nafter the victim was seen...": "",
  "...And that's Okubo-san himself!": "",
  "...Was the man you're defending!": "",
  "Are you saying he really is the culprit?": "",
  "So that means he <font_kind=yakuza_italic>is</font_kind> the culprit\nafter all, right?": "",
  "Huh? I, um...": "",
  "Huh? Wait, hold on...": "",
  "The one who killed Waku-san...\nis actually our witness, Shono-san.": "",
  "The real culprit in Waku-san's murder\nis Shono-san, the witness.": "",
  "Excuse me? What grounds do you\nhave for that assertion!?": "",
  "Huh...? Wait, what!?\nWhat basis do you have for that?": "",
  "Grounds? Grounds... Um, well...": "",
  "Basis? My basis is...\nUh, you see...": "",
  "Sorry. Let me start over.": "",
  "My apologies. Let me start over.": "",
  "The witness, Shono-san, said that\nWaku-san was sleeping in his room.": "",
  "However, I'm not convinced\nthat's actually what happened.": "",
  "However, it should be impossible\nfor him to testify to that.": "",
  "Correct. As such, there's no way he could have known\nwhether or not it was Waku-san in the bed.": "",
  "Shono-san was lying when he said\nhe saw Waku-san in the bed.": "",
  "Shono-san testified that he saw Waku-san,\nbut that's untrue.": "",
  "Excuse me?": "",
  "What he saw from the door was likely\nnothing more than a bulge of sheets.": "",
  "Shono-san believes he saw someone,\nbut what he saw was not necessarily Waku-san.": "",
  "He couldn't have been able to identify\nit specifically as Waku-san.": "",
  "The sheets could have been\nruffled for all he knew.": "",
  "So, to claim as much in his testimony\nseems like quite an exaggeration, don't you think?": "",
  "Despite that, testifying that he saw Waku-san sleeping\nis quite an exaggeration.": "",
  "But common sense would dictate otherwise, would it not?\nWho would be in the bed other than Waku-san?": "",
  "How so? It would be common sense\nto suppose Waku-san is in his own bed.": "",
  "The staff nurses are trained to always enter\na room when checking in on a patient.": "",
  "In our training as nurses, we always enter a room\nwhen checking in on a patient.": "",
  "And in the course of a day,\nhow often does a nurse visit each patient?": "",
  "At least ten times a day on average.": "",
  "Even in the middle of the night, we'll go in\nevery three hours or so to change their diapers.": "",
  "Patients will sometimes call for a nurse's assistance\noutside of our regular check-ins as well.": "",
  "And you always walk into the room?": "",
  "In Waku-san's case, it's impossible to tell\nanything just by looking in from the hallway.": "",
  "In Waku-san's case, it's impossible to tell\njust by looking in from the hallway.": "",
  "There was actually one time a while back\nwhere we thought he was under the covers...": "",
  "In one instance, we believed we saw him\nunder the covers in his room...": "",
  "Only to find Waku-san eating\nin the break room a second later.": "",
  "...Only to find him eating\nin the day room a second later.": "",
  "And upon re-examining the room, we realized\nthat we had mistaken a bunched-up pillow for Waku-san.": "",
  "After we entered the room ourselves to check,\nwe realized it had just been a bunched-up pillow.": "",
  "The witness makes an important distinction.": "",
  "Our witness makes an important point.": "",
  "The prosecution asserts that\nShono-san's testimony is clear.": "",
  "The prosecution asserts that\na clear timeframe exists.": "",
  "That the victim was taken out of his room\nat some point between 7:50 and 8:30 in the morning.": "",
  "By Shono-san's account, the victim was removed at some point\nbetween 7:50 and 8:30 in the morning.": "",
  "They claim that because of this time frame, the defendant must\nhave smuggled Waku-san's body out in his laundry bin.": "",
  "Based on this testimony, they suggest the defendant\nsmuggled Waku-san's body out in a laundry cart.": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(That's why Okubo-kun was assumed to be\nthe only person who could have killed Waku-san.)</color>": "",
  "But if Shono-san's testimony is invalid,\nas the defense asserts...": "",
  "But if Shono-san's testimony\nis thrown into question...": "",
  "We have to consider the possibility that Waku-san\nwas taken in the middle of the night, when nobody else was around.": "",
  "...Then there is another possibility: That Waku-san was taken\nin the middle of the night, with nobody to see it.": "",
  "After which the killer could have waited until\nmorning to plant the body in the defendant's truck.": "",
  "After which, the killer could have waited until the morning\nto plant the body in the defendant's truck.": "",
  "In other words, the defense establishes that\nthere is reasonable doubt that Okubo-san is the killer.": "",
  "In other words, it's entirely possible that Waku-san was murdered\nby someone other than Okubo-san here.": "",
  "Rendering the prosecution's\ncentral argument unsound.": "",
  "Your Honor. Taking this new testimony into account, I'd like\nto call Shono-san back to the stand for cross-examination.": "",
  "Your Honor. Taking this new testimony into account,\nI'd like to recall Shono-san to the stand for cross-examination.": "",
  "Shono-san.": "",
  "<color=ｍonologue>(Let's see how Shono responds with that evidence\nand Terasawa-san's testimony out in the open.)</color>": "",
  "I'll get right to the point.": "",
  "Allow me to get right to the point.": "",
  "On the day of the crime, what did you see\nwhen you looked into Waku-san's room?": "",
  "I saw Waku-san asleep in his bed...\nI think.": "",
  "I believe... I saw Waku-san\nasleep in his bed.": "",
  "And did you get a clear look\nat his face?": "",
  "And did you get a clear look\nat Waku-san's face?": "",
  "I don't remember.": "",
  "So it's possible that it could have been\nsomeone other than Waku-san in that bed?": "",
  "So it's possible that the person in the bed\nwas someone else entirely.": "",
  "Or maybe even a pillow that you mistook\nto be Waku-san's body?": "",
  "Or maybe even a pillow\nthat you mistook to be Waku-san's body.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "What the hell's your problem!?": "มึงมีปัญหาอะไรวะ!?",
  "Let go of me!": "ปล่อยฉันนะ!",
  "And this is...?": "แล้วท่านนี้คือ...?",
  "What are you implying?": "นายจะสื่ออะไร?",
  "Huh? Wait, hold on...": "หา? เดี๋ยว เดี๋ยวก่อน...",
  "Excuse me?": "ว่าไงนะ?",
